      "id": 1,
      "text": "Morgan began in 1861 as North Morgan, originally called Mount Joy by early settlers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morgan%2C_Utah",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city honors Jedediah Morgan Grant, an LDS apostle who helped settle the valley and build Weber Canyon’s first road.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morgan%2C_Utah",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Union Pacific’s 1868-69 tracks through Weber Canyon put Morgan on the map as a railroad town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morgan%2C_Utah",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The 1989 horror film Troll 2 was filmed mostly in and around Morgan, giving the town a cult movie legacy.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
